    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Root Cause:** The `--ci` flag was defined on the main `frai` program. When running `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was parsing `--ci` at the main program level before the gate subcommand could receive it. The args passed to the gate action handler only contained `['init']` without the `--ci` flag.\n\n**Solution Applied:** Three changes to `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d04/with/t1-flag-bug/r2/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. **Added `.enablePositionalOptions(true)` to the main program** (line 603) - This allows subcommands to receive options that would normally be parsed at the main level.\n\n2. **Added `.passThroughOptions(true)` to the gate command** (line 742) - This tells Commander to pass through unrecognized options to the action handler rather than parsing them.\n\n3. **Modified the gate action handler** (lines 744-766) - Now extracts options from the command object and includes them in the args passed to the frai-gate CLI:\n   - Collects all positional args\n   - Iterates through the command options\n   - Reconstructs flags in the format `--flag` or `--flag value`\n   - Passes the complete args to frai-gate\n\n**Verification:** Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested that `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe changes ensure that all flags and options passed to the `frai gate` command are properly forwarded to the underlying frai-gate CLI.",
